 ## Overview
-A multi-planar volumetric 3D display projects a sequence of 2D image patterns onto a screen moving along the Z-axis to form a stack of spatial image planes, creating a true 3D image viewable without glasses [S1]. Unlike conventional 2D screens that rely on psychological depth cues, this method places voxels at their physical spatial positions, emitting light omni-directionally to provide both physiological and psychological depth cues [S1]. Builds on [Rotational Swept-Screen Projection](8589-rotational-swept-screen-projection.md). It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [Volumetric Display using Rotating Mirror (VRDM)](2567-volumetric-display-using-rotating-mirror-vrdm.md), [2D Full-Color LED Array Rotational Display](7246-2d-full-color-led-array-rotational-display.md), and [Oscillating Swept Volume Display](15668-oscillating-swept-volume-display.md) by utilizing linear or reciprocating screen motion rather than rotational sweep [G].
+A multi-planar volumetric 3D display projects a sequence of 2D image patterns onto a screen moving along the Z-axis to form a stack of spatial image planes, creating a true 3D image viewable without glasses [S1]. Unlike conventional 2D screens that rely on psychological depth cues, this method places voxels at their physical spatial positions, emitting light omni-directionally to provide both physiological and psychological depth cues [S1]. Builds on [Rotational Swept-Screen Projection](8589-rotational-swept-screen-projection.md) [G]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [Volumetric Display using Rotating Mirror (VRDM)](2567-volumetric-display-using-rotating-mirror-vrdm.md), [2D Full-Color LED Array Rotational Display](7246-2d-full-color-led-array-rotational-display.md), and [Oscillating Swept Volume Display](15668-oscillating-swept-volume-display.md) by utilizing linear or reciprocating screen motion rather than rotational sweep [G].
 
